    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0753" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Matthews Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        Matthews Notes</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d347-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Leningrad</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-chapter-heading" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1945-02-06T12:00:00+03:00">February 6, 1945, noon</date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">1. Communiqué<anchor n="2" xml:id="d347-f2"/>—S.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d347-f3"/> thinks wise to issue one</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mol</hi>. Preliminary One suggestion: add <hi
                        rendition="#underline">“common”</hi> enemy. Likes communiqué. No objection
                    to mention Black Sea area. Must be approved by Stalin
                </p>
                <p rendition="#flush">2. S. announces 3 questions before the 3 F. M. On first
                    point.</p>
                <p>Adding “dismemberment” to Art 12<anchor n="4" xml:id="d347-f4"/> &amp; refer to
                        EAC.</p>
                <pb facs="0754" n="658" xml:id="pg658"/>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mol</hi>. Accepts addition of word.</p>
                <p>
                    
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Eden</hi>. Another formula “and
                    measures for the dissolution of the German unitary state” Would cover abolition
                    of centralization of Germ. govt.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mol</hi>: Will exercise sup.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d347-f5"/> power . . .<anchor n="6" xml:id="d347-f6"/> take measures
                    for dismemberment of G. For peace &amp; security of Europe necessary to
                    dismember G.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>Agreed to add: “And the dismemberment” after demilitarization.</p>
                    <p>No agreement on Russian change.</p>
                </quote>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d347-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d347-f1-content">
                <p>Transcribed for this volume from longhand notes in pencil.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d347-f2" n="2" xml:id="d347-f2-content">
                <p>For citations to pertinent documents, see the preceding Page minutes of this meeting.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d347-f3" n="3" xml:id="d347-f3-content">
                <p>
                    Stettinius. (Throughout the Matthews notes the editors have added footnote
                    explanations of the more unusual contractions and abbreviations.)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d347-f4" n="4" xml:id="d347-f4-content">
                <p>Of the draft instrument entitled “Unconditional Surrender of Germany”.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d347-f5" n="5" xml:id="d347-f5-content">
                <p>supreme.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d347-f6" n="6" xml:id="d347-f6-content">
                <p>Points appear in the original.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
